      "claim": "Jupiter has no true surface; extreme pressures and temperatures crush, melt and vaporise spacecraft; deep inside, hydrogen becomes electrically conducting like metal; Juno suggests the core is not solid, partially dissolved, described as dilute or fuzzy; radius 69,911 km",
